<title>RUSSIA: Russia's 210-day T-bill yield falls to 32.59 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia's 210-day T-bill yield falls to 32.59 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 210-day GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 32.59 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 41.06 percent at an auction of 203-day paper on December 11, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction:</p>
<p>					Dec 25	     Dec 11</p>
<p>    Series number		 22064		22062</p>
<p>    Issue volume		  7.50 trln rbls   8.50 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		 1.00 million	   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		9.42 trln	 10.46 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		6.31 trln	  8.20 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			5.31 trln	  6.67 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		84.21 pct	  81.41 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price    84.00 pct	  80.75 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		32.59 pct	  41.06 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield   33.11 pct	  42.86 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			   210 days	   203 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		 July 23, 1997    July 2, 1997</p>
<p>The finance ministry also repaid 6.07 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills (series 22037).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
